<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        ADDED 2026-08-25 (native LOI/PSA Details, scope addition). THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE
        ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY - a comment above &lt;CustomField&gt; breaks `sf` at source
        conversion with a misleading "unable to find matching parent xml file" error.

        A LINK, NOT A COPY. Someone working the LOI needs to open the Disposition_Offer__c row
        the deal was actually built on - the buyer, the offer amount, the counter history - and
        today the only route is up to the Disposition and back down its offers related list.
        This lookup is that route in one click. Nothing is denormalised onto the LOI: the offer's
        own fields stay on the offer.

        🔴 IT IS STAMPED ONTO THE CHILD AT INSERT, WHICH IS WHY IT NEEDS NO QUEUEABLE. This field
        is set on the row being created, in the same Database.insert, by
        DispositionStageEntryService.openDispositionLois.
        ⚠ AMENDED 2026-08-25 AND UN-AMENDED 2026-08-26. The sentence above originally contrasted
        this with "Disposition__c.Primary_LOI__c in the same change: that one writes BACK to the
        parent mid-save and must be deferred". On 2026-08-25 that lookup was deleted with the
        child-mirror family and the contrast was re-pointed at Disposition__c.Primary_NDA__c. On
        2026-08-26 the user restored both lookups (option A - rebuild the Details sections on
        SPANNING items, leave the 15 formula mirrors deleted), so THE ORIGINAL CONTRAST IS LIVE
        AGAIN: Primary_LOI__c writes back to the parent and is deferred to
        DispositionPrimaryChildStampQueueable; this field is stamped in-line on the child.
        Primary_NDA__c works the same way and is an equally good contrast.
        🔴 THIS FIELD WAS NEVER AFFECTED BY EITHER SWING AND WAS DELIBERATELY LEFT IN PLACE
        THROUGHOUT. It lives on LOI__c, not on Disposition__c, and it is a navigational link to a
        real child record rather than a mirrored copy of one - which is the distinction both of
        the user's decisions turned on.

        ⚠ NULL IS A NORMAL, NON-ERROR STATE AND THE INSERT MUST NEVER BLOCK ON IT. A disposition
        can legitimately reach the LOI stage with no selected offer (an off-market deal that
        never ran an offer round), and every acquisition LOI - which has no Disposition__c at
        all - carries null here forever. Anything reading this field must handle blank.

        deleteConstraint SetNull: deleting an offer clears the pointer, never cascades into the
        LOI. relationshipName Selected_Offer_LOIs, distinct from the Contract_Review__c twin's
        Selected_Offer_PSAs so the two child relationships on Disposition_Offer__c do not collide.

        FLS: read + edit on DPEG_Disposition_Edit (a lookup CAN carry editable = true, and a user
        working a hand-created second-round LOI may need to set the link), read-only on
        DPEG_Disposition_View.
        ⚠ THE OTHER HALF OF THAT REASON - a one-off backfill needing USER-mode edit - NEVER
        APPLIED TO THIS FIELD AND STILL DOES NOT. It belongs to the Disposition__c lookups, whose
        backfill was retired on 2026-08-25 and came back on 2026-08-26 as
        scripts/backfill-disposition-primary-children.apex. That script's DML is PLAIN (anonymous
        Apex cannot use SYSTEM_MODE), so it does still need the edit grant - on Primary_LOI__c /
        Primary_PSA__c, not here. NOTHING BACKFILLS THIS FIELD: it has only ever been stamped at
        insert.
    -->
    <fullName>Selected_Offer__c</fullName>
    <deleteConstraint>SetNull</deleteConstraint>
    <description>The selected Disposition Offer this LOI was raised against - stamped when the LOI is auto-created. Blank on acquisition LOIs and on dispositions that never ran an offer round.</description>
    <inlineHelpText>Opens the buyer offer this LOI came from. Set automatically when the LOI is created; blank if the disposition had no selected offer.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Selected Offer</label>
    <referenceTo>Disposition_Offer__c</referenceTo>
    <relationshipLabel>LOIs (Selected Offer)</relationshipLabel>
    <relationshipName>Selected_Offer_LOIs</relationshipName>
    <required>false</required>
    <trackFeedHistory>false</trackFeedHistory>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Lookup</type>
</CustomField>
